# Convex CLI target — apps/api/.env.local
# Convex cloud: `npx convex dev` writes CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT (and CONVEX_URL) here.
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=
# Self-hosted / local backend instead:
# CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3210
# CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_ADMIN_KEY=

# Deployment env — NOT read from this file. Set each with
#   cd apps/api && npx convex env set NAME value
#
# Required:
#   CONVEX_SERVICE_TOKEN          same value as the root .env (worker auth)
# LLM fallback for chat / enhance when no provider is saved in Settings:
#   LLM_PROVIDER, LLM_MODEL, LLM_BASE_URL (or LLM_OPENAI_BASE_URL /
#   LLM_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL), LLM_API_KEY
#   PROVIDER_ENCRYPTION_KEY       encrypts provider keys saved in Settings
#                                 (same value as the root .env)
# Optional:
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_ID, GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET   GitHub OAuth app (push / draft PR)
#   GITHUB_OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL     default http://localhost:3000/api/integrations/github/callback
#   OAUTH_STATE_SECRET            HMAC key for the signed one-time OAuth state;
#                                 falls back to PROVIDER_ENCRYPTION_KEY
#   APP_ORIGIN                    web app origin the OAuth popup posts to;
#                                 default: origin of GITHUB_OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL
#   (The GitHub token is stored encrypted, so connecting GitHub needs
#    PROVIDER_ENCRYPTION_KEY.)
#   GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET         fallback webhook secret (per-project secrets
#                                 from Integrations win); none = webhooks 401
#   MOAGENT_WEEKLY_TOKEN_BUDGET   weekly token budget shown in the usage meter
